    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is an online competitive game where players leave the girls of Gensokyo behind and compete to see who has the best relationships.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Specifically, like in \u201cFive in a Row,\u201d players place characters as stones in a straight line to increase their total points (the number needed to win).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >However, since the goal is to compete for the best relationships, the characters placed next to each other must be friends.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Abilities</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each character has unique abilities, such as \u201cplacing multiple stones in one move\u201d or \u201cdestroying the opponent's stones,\u201d among others.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In particular, the \u201cSpell Card,\u201d which can be used once per match, is extremely powerful, and its usage can significantly influence the outcome of the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u2606This game is a fan-made game based on the Touhou Project.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is an online competitive game where players leave the girls of Gensokyo behind and compete to see who has the best relationships.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Specifically, like in \u201cFive in a Row,\u201d players place characters as stones in a straight line to increase their total points (the number needed to win).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >However, since the goal is to compete for the best relationships, the characters placed next to each other must be friends.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Abilities</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each character has unique abilities, such as \u201cplacing multiple stones in one move\u201d or \u201cdestroying the opponent's stones,\u201d among others.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In particular, the \u201cSpell Card,\u201d which can be used once per match, is extremely powerful, and its usage can significantly influence the outcome of the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u2606This game is a fan-made game based on the Touhou Project.</p>",
    "short_description": "An online battle game where you place girls from Gensokyo like in a game of Go! However, since the goal is to compete based on how well they get along, you can only win when the girls next to each other are friends. Enjoy the strategies created by their abilities and relationships!",
